# SRG-APP-000805-AU-000240  -  CAT II
# The Central Log Server must automatically generate audit records of the
# enforcement actions.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000805-AU-000240
group:           V-263570
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-003938
control_rev5:    CM-5

contribution:    Splunk records its own enforcement actions in two places it controls: the
                 configuration change log, which captures every change to a .conf file
                 including the values that changed, and the audit trail, which it can queue
                 to an index so the records are searchable and retained.

governs:         audit.conf - The audit trail Splunk keeps of its own activity, and how those records
                 are signed.
governs:         server.conf - Core server settings, including the certificates and protocols used to
                 protect management and replication traffic.

check:           server.conf [config_change_tracker] disabled in false|0
check:           server.conf [config_change_tracker] mode in auto|diff
check:           audit.conf [auditTrail] queueing in true|1
check:           server.conf [config_change_tracker] denylist absent
check:           server.conf [config_change_tracker] exclude_fields absent
check:           server.conf [config_change_tracker] log_throttling_disabled in true|1

external:        Enforcement actions taken outside the application - operating system
                 access control decisions, firewall denials, directory service lockouts -
                 carried by those components and recorded by them.
external:        Retention, protection, and off-host copy of the records once written,
                 which the AU family assesses rather than this requirement.
external:        Individual change logging requires a Linux host with the inotify file
                 system event interface, which is a platform property.

citation:        Central Log Server SRG SRG-APP-000805-AU-000240 check and fix text;
                 server.conf.spec:599 (config_change_tracker disabled, default false),
                 server.conf.spec:608 (mode = [auto|diff|track-only], default auto),
                 server.conf.spec:636 (denylist, no default), server.conf.spec:641
                 (log_throttling_disabled, default true), server.conf.spec:661
                 (exclude_fields), audit.conf.spec:24 (queueing, default true)
finding:         Configuration change tracking is switched off, set to track-only, narrowed
                 by a denylist or excluded fields, or the audit trail is not queued to an
                 index, so the application does not automatically generate a complete
                 record of its own enforcement actions.
